{"text": "Certainly!", "start": 0, "end": 10, "label": "accept"}
{"text": "Let's try to get to the target number 24 using the numbers 6, 8, 10, and 12 exactly once with the operations +, -, *, and /.", "start": 11, "end": 135, "label": "suggest"}
{"text": "One of the ways to achieve this is:", "start": 137, "end": 172, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(12 - 8) × (10 + 6) = 4 × 16 = 64 div 2 = 24", "start": 174, "end": 218, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "However, we need to make sure all numbers are used exactly once.", "start": 220, "end": 284, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "We can also use a bit simpler approach:", "start": 285, "end": 324, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(10 - 6) × (12 div 8) × 4 = 4 × 1.5 × 4 = 12 × 2 = 24", "start": 326, "end": 379, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "This can be simplified further by reorganizing the operations:", "start": 381, "end": 443, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(10 - 6) × left((12/8)right) × 4 = 4 × 1.5 × 4 = 6 × 4 = 24", "start": 445, "end": 504, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "But the simplest effective method:", "start": 506, "end": 540, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(12 - 6) × (10 div 8) × 4 = 6 × 1.25 × 4 = 3 × 10 = 30 quad (This won't work)", "start": 542, "end": 619, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Let's try another combination:", "start": 621, "end": 651, "label": "suggest"}
{"text": "12 × (10 div 8) - 6 = 12 × 1.25 - 6 = 15 - 6 = 24", "start": 653, "end": 702, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Yes, this works.", "start": 704, "end": 720, "label": "confirm"}
{"text": "So the solution is:", "start": 721, "end": 740, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "12 × left((10/8)right) - 6 = 12 × 1.25 - 6 = 15 - 6 = 24", "start": 799, "end": 855, "label": "inform"}
